<description>
Expand the input into a block grid equal to the self-product of its black-cell mask.

Input structure
- The input is a non-empty 2D grid with black background cells and exactly one foreground color.
- Every output block has the same height and width as the input.

Rule
- Treat the black cells of the input as a binary mask.
- Replace each black input cell by that same black-cell mask, recolored with the foreground color.
- Replace each foreground input cell by an all-black block.

Key insight
The enlarged output mask is the Kronecker product of the input's black-cell mask with itself.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "input black-cell mask plus the single foreground color",
  "transform": "take the Kronecker product of the black-cell mask with itself; recolor true cells with the foreground color and false cells black",
  "grid_shape": "H x W input -> (H*H) x (W*W) output"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 3x3 input -> 9x9 output
  colors: black background + exactly 1 foreground color (any non-black)
  black_cells: 3-5 out of 9 cells are black; remaining are foreground
  mask: binary mask M where M[r,c]=1 iff cell is black
  constraint: at least 1 black and 1 foreground cell (solver asserts both)
  output: Kronecker product M kron M; true cells get foreground color, false cells black
  #  Input example:        Black mask:     Output = kron(mask, mask) recolored
  #  [[fg fg 0 ]           [[0 0 1]        Each black cell -> copy of mask in fg
  #   [0  fg fg]            [1 0 0]        Each fg cell    -> 3x3 all-black block
  #   [0  fg 0 ]]           [1 0 1]]

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct (input is small 3x3; output is deterministic)
  steps:
    - pick foreground color uniformly from non-black ARC colors
    - generate a random 3x3 binary mask with 3-5 true (black) cells
    - build input grid: black where mask=1, foreground where mask=0
```
</generation_spec>
</reference_puzzle>

